## 11. DATASET PARTITIONING AND VERSIONING

Implement deterministic dataset releases.

### 11.1 Dataset release types

- TRAIN.
- VALIDATION.
- TEST.
- CHALLENGE.
- REGRESSION.
- STREAMING_EVALUATION.
- RESEARCH_ONLY.

Keep the authoritative benchmark test set protected.

Training pipelines must not have unrestricted access to sealed test transcripts.

### 11.2 Initial 30-hour dataset plan

The initial project planning target is approximately 30 hours.

The previously proposed split was:

- Training: 21 hours.
- Validation: 3 hours.
- Test: 6 hours.

Treat these as initial planning targets rather than mandatory quantities.

The actual split must respect speaker, session, language, and source-group constraints.

If the corpus cannot support all required group-disjoint partitions, explicitly report the limitation.

Do not force a mathematically convenient split that introduces speaker leakage.

### 11.3 Expansion milestones

Use the following as dataset growth planning checkpoints:

| Milestone | Approximate cumulative duration | Purpose |
|---|---:|---|
| D0 | 30 hours | Pipeline validation and baseline experiments |
| D1 | 100 hours | Early data diversity assessment |
| D2 | 500 hours | More meaningful fine-tuning research |
| D3 | 2,000 hours | Broader model adaptation experiments |
| D4 | 10,000 hours | Larger-scale training research |

These are project planning milestones, not universal thresholds guaranteeing model quality.

Track useful and approved duration, not merely uploaded duration.

### 11.4 Dataset version manifest

Every release must have:

- Dataset ID.
