## 14. BENCHMARK DATASET PROTECTION

Maintain a strict boundary between training and final evaluation.

### 14.1 Protected test set

Implement:

- Restricted read access.
- Separate storage permissions where appropriate.
- Audit logging.
- Controlled evaluation service.
- Test-manifest integrity.
- Versioned reference transcripts.
- Leakage monitoring.

Only authorized evaluation workflows should access sealed reference transcripts.

### 14.2 Benchmark contamination

Detect whether evaluation samples have appeared in:

- Training manifests.
- Fine-tuning manifests.
- Public sample collections used for model adaptation.
- Previously distributed development datasets.

Record source dataset lineage.

Where contamination cannot be ruled out, label the evaluation limitation honestly.

### 14.3 Reproducible evaluation

Each benchmark run must bind:

- Dataset version.
- Dataset split.
- Model version.
- Inference configuration.
- Language-normalization policy.
- Scoring library version.
- Hardware environment.
- Execution timestamp.

Never compare two WER or CER values produced with different normalization policies without explicitly explaining the difference.

