- Review.
- Adjudication.

Exit criterion: a real recording can pass through a complete human-verified annotation workflow with preserved history.

### PHASE 12D — Dataset Versioning and Leakage Prevention

- Dataset manifests.
- Split policies.
- Speaker grouping.
- Duplicate audits.
- Immutable releases.
- Benchmark protection.

Exit criterion: a reproducible dataset release can be built and its split integrity can be audited.

### PHASE 12E — Training and Evaluation Integration

- Training manifest export.
- Evaluation manifest export.
- Existing benchmark pipeline integration.
- Dataset lineage.
- Regression datasets.
- Reproducible experiment linkage.

Exit criterion: an actual training or evaluation run can identify exactly which approved dataset release and artifact versions it consumed.

### PHASE 12F — Data Quality Operations

- Dataset dashboard.
- Quality metrics.
- Diversity reporting.
- Rights reporting.
- Annotation throughput.
- Defect monitoring.
- Data drift analysis.

Exit criterion: operators can identify dataset weaknesses using real recorded measurements rather than manually maintained estimates.

