## 21. DEFINITION OF DONE

Phase 12 must not be marked complete because a data upload endpoint or annotation interface exists.

It is complete only when:

1. Audio can be ingested through a real processing pipeline.
2. Original audio remains immutable.
3. Transformed artifacts have traceable provenance.
4. Rights and consent are enforced.
5. Metadata is validated.
6. Audio quality is measured.
7. Duplicate detection operates.
8. Annotation history is preserved.
9. Persian and English policies are implemented.
10. Code-switching can be represented.
11. Dataset releases are immutable and reproducible.
12. Speaker and session leakage audits operate.
13. Benchmark references are protected.
14. Data deletion and revocation workflows are tested.
15. Existing ASR benchmark and training pipelines can consume approved releases.
16. Security tests pass.
17. Documentation matches the real implementation.
18. Known limitations are disclosed.

Report each milestone independently:

- COMPLETE_AND_VERIFIED
- IMPLEMENTED_UNVERIFIED
- PARTIAL
- BLOCKED
- NOT_STARTED

Do not report total uploaded hours as useful training hours.

Report separately:

- Uploaded duration.
- Validated duration.
- Rights-approved duration.
- Annotated duration.
- Reviewed duration.
- Training-eligible duration.
- Evaluation-eligible duration.

