## 22. EXECUTION RULES

Inspect the existing repository before designing new components.

Reuse healthy ingestion, storage, database, and security infrastructure.

Do not create duplicate data platforms.

Do not collect unnecessary personal information.

Do not use unauthorized public audio.

Do not mix training and protected evaluation data.

Do not automatically treat ASR output as ground truth.

Do not allow automated annotations to become approved reference transcripts without the defined quality gate.

Do not claim dataset quality based only on duration.

Do not claim legal compliance without suitable evidence and review.

Do not silently discard difficult or noisy samples.

Do not execute expensive data collection, paid annotation, or external storage provisioning without authorization.

After each milestone, run relevant tests, inspect changes, record evidence, and update the persistent execution state.

When the user says continue, resume from the first incomplete and executable dependency.

**PRIMARY OBJECTIVE: Build a legally authorized, high-quality, diverse, reproducible, versioned, and independently auditable Persian-English speech corpus infrastructure that can reliably support the entire ASR research and production lifecycle.**